 "notes": "Relic dark-photon DM absorption limit from Fig. 15 (top panel), the solid dark-blue 'XENON1T SE (This Work)' 90% CL curve, extracted from the vector paths of the e-print figure fig_bosonic_limits.pdf and calibrated against the axis tick marks (log-log). This is the paper's reported conservative limit assuming ionization from the lowest accessible electron shell; the blue shaded band in the figure is the systematic from the alternative outermost-5p-shell assumption and is not reported here. Chosen as the main result because the abstract highlights excluding new parameter space for dark photons (the ALP g_ae limit in the bottom panel does not exceed prior bounds; the solar dark-photon limit of Fig. 16 is a separate non-DM flux result). The near-vertical rise at threshold (~12.1 eV, xenon 5p binding) was clipped at the plot frame, giving the first point (11.4 eV, 5.0e-13). Local DM density is not stated numerically in the paper; 0.3 GeV/cm^3 (the standard XENON halo-model value) is assumed. Masses converted from keV/c^2 to eV.",
